[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One Unix socket carries newline-framed JSON-RPC to the workspace

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-RPC
TITLE: One Unix socket carries newline-framed JSON-RPC to the workspace
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Requests reach the workspace as JSON-RPC 2.0, one JSON value per newline, over
an AF_UNIX stream socket at mode 0600 inside a directory at mode 0700 owned by
the caller.

THE ENVELOPE IS pjrpc'S, THE TRANSPORT IS OURS. A synchronous, framework-free
pjrpc Dispatcher owns request parsing, the id and version rules, method lookup,
batch handling and error serialization. The socket, the newline framing, the
16 MiB request cap, the threading server, the derived socket path, the
ownership probe and the no-fallback rule remain this repository's.

Every method is registered with a pydantic contract built from its signature,
forbidding extra keys and refusing a value of the wrong JSON type, so an
unknown parameter or a string where a bool was declared is -32602 naming the
field rather than a key that is quietly dropped. Which parameters a given
OPERATION requires, and which it forbids, is a second layer: one model per
operation, beside the operations themselves. Refusals keep their codes --
-32001 for a workspace that could not answer, -32002 for an operation that was
understood and declined.

A request over the cap is drained before its refusal is written, so the client
receives the refusal instead of a broken pipe. Batches are accepted up to eight
requests and refused above that, because the daemon serializes every write
behind one held graph.

On start the server probes any socket already at its path: refused or absent
means stale and it is replaced; a successful connect means another daemon owns
this workspace and the start fails. On stop the socket is removed only if its
inode is the one that was bound.

rpc.discover reports the schema -- `scribe-rpc/2` since the envelope moved onto
pjrpc -- the framing, the served root, and the method list READ OFF THE
REGISTRY, so what exists and what is advertised cannot drift apart. Every
method that answers about the workspace names the root it served, and the
client refuses any reply that is not a well-formed JSON-RPC response, a result
that is not an object included, rather than indexing into it.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Retained from the retired RPC-and-service delivery row on 2026-09-10: daemon
hydration completes before the socket is bound
(dev/scripts/scribe_daemon.py calls workspace.current() before build_server()).
The socket's existence is therefore the readiness signal: a client checks by
connecting rather than by polling a second state surface.
<<<
